# Scope Policy

Import and export are in place. This file is the current product boundary. Plugin kind definitions and execution shape live in `16-plugins.mdc`.

## In scope

Design and implement these. A plugin contract is cut at the first real caller. A later plugin of the same kind uses that contract.

| Item | Boundary |
|---|---|
| projection, writer-filter, adapter-target | In-repo plugins. How many stages run, and how often a target runs, is in `16-plugins.mdc` |
| Domain validation | Invariants of one IR kind, in a named module beside that kind. Raw boundary schema stays. No rule DSL |
| IR schema migration | Versioned transforms when a snapshot or IR shape change is not additive. An additive field does not add a transform |

## Still out

| Item | Use instead |
|---|---|
| Event bus | Direct calls, Context, stores, ordered filter pipelines |
| Undo / Redo command stack | Snapshot `current` / `history` / `versions` |
| Service framework | Use-case modules and the plugin pipeline runners that already have a caller |
| Untrusted plugins | In-repo registry only. No `eval`, no out-of-repo `import`, no marketplace, no PluginHost |
| Shared Plugin base class | Wait until three hosts share the same code |
| Empty hosts | A host ships with a concrete plugin |
